@startuml
!include theme.iuml
title Operator background backup — one due shared-workspace cycle
hide footbox
autonumber
participant "main.py lifespan" as App
participant "maintain_backups()\nmaintenance_cycle()" as Worker
participant "snapshot()/build_archive()\nworkspace_backups.py" as Backup
participant "store : SharedWorkspaceStore\nsystem=True" as Store
participant "Private audio / backup files" as Files
activate App
App -> Worker : maintain_backups(data_dir, stop)
activate Worker
note over Worker : Poll in threadpool; this view shows one shared-workspace cycle.\nWhen shared storage is absent, retained private stores are considered instead.
create Store
Worker -> Store : SharedWorkspaceStore(data_dir, SYSTEM_OWNER_ID,\n"System", system=True)
activate Store
Store --> Worker : privileged internal store
deactivate Store
Worker -> Store : lock(); get_metadata(settings/state) via connection()
activate Store
Store --> Worker : automatic schedule and prior attempts/success
deactivate Store
opt automatic enabled and interval/retry timing is due
  Worker -> Backup : snapshot(store, kind="automatic")
  activate Backup
  Backup -> Store : export_document()
  activate Store
  Store --> Backup : logical shared format-5 document
  deactivate Store
  Backup -> Files : read all safe audio files;\ncheck referenced media and size limits
  activate Files
  Files --> Backup : audio bytes, or explicit storage error
  deactivate Files
  opt archive construction succeeds
    Backup -> Backup : validate_archive(new ZIP + checksum manifest)
    activate Backup
    Backup --> Backup : verified archive, or rejection
    deactivate Backup
    opt archive validated and disk quota allows publication
      Backup -> Files : atomic_write(generated backup ZIP path, data)
      activate Files
      Files --> Backup : published
      deactivate Files
      Backup -> Store : set_metadata("backup:item:" + id, entry)
      activate Store
      Store --> Backup : catalogue record, or error
      deactivate Store
    end
  end
  Backup --> Worker : verified backup entry, or explicit failure
  deactivate Backup
  note over Worker : On success: retain keep_last automatic copies and record last_success.\nOn failure: log safely, record last_error if possible; never claim success.\nIf catalogue insertion failed, snapshot() removes the just-published ZIP.
end
note over Worker : Release locks. Wait up to 60 seconds, then repeat unless stop is set.
Worker --> App : return when lifespan stop event is set
deactivate Worker
deactivate App
legend bottom
  No public backup API or recovery screen is mounted; maintenance can run privately in public mode.
  Default automatic=false; configured intervals are 24/168 hours and keep_last is 1..10.
  This backup preserves workspace/media, not auth.sqlite3 or /etc/camfranglais.env.
  Archive validation and atomic file publication precede a successful catalogue entry.
endlegend
@enduml
